<Base title="Travel guide" description="Practical starting points for planning a Tamil Nadu journey, choosing a season and visiting respectfully.">
<PageHeading label="BEFORE YOU SET OFF" title="A little planning.<br/>More room to wander." description="Choose a region, check the season and leave space between the stops. Start here, then make the details your own."/><section class="guide-notes wrap"><article><span class="meta">CHOOSE A BASE</span><h2>One region at a time.</h2><p>Start with a compact Mamallapuram break, an Ooty base, or a longer Madurai and Rameswaram journey. Allow for the trip to your first destination and your onward connection.</p><a class="text-link" href="/routes/">Compare the routes</a></article><article><span class="meta">GETTING AROUND</span><h2>Let the journey breathe.</h2><p>Check rail and bus connections directly with your chosen operator. Hill roads, weather and local traffic can change a travel day. Keep a buffer between arrival and your first planned visit.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.irctc.co.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Indian Railways booking</a></article><article><span class="meta">VISITING WITH CARE</span><h2>Follow the place's lead.</h2><p>Check temple entry, dress and photography rules before your visit. Ask before photographing people, follow local instructions and keep to permitted paths at coastal and hill destinations.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.tamilnadutourism.tn.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tamil Nadu Tourism</a></article><article><span class="meta">PACK FOR YOUR ROUTE</span><h2>Small things, useful days.</h2><p>Comfortable walking shoes, sun protection and a refillable water bottle help on city days. Add a light layer for the hills and rain protection when conditions call for it.</p><button class="text-link" data-plan>Make a personal trip brief</button></article></section><SeasonGuide/><TravelFaq/>
</Base>
